TESTING & DEBUGGING
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  sudo mount -a              Test all fstab entries
  sudo mount -a -v           Verbose output
  findmnt --verify           Check fstab for problems
  systemctl daemon-reload    After changing fstab with systemd options
  journalctl -xe             Check for mount errors
  dmesg | tail               Kernel messages related to mounts

QUICK REFERENCE
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  UUID=...                   Prefer over /dev/sdX (stable)
  _netdev                    Always use for network mounts
  nofail                     Prevent boot hang if share unavailable
  x-systemd.automount        Mount only when accessed
  mount -a                   Apply fstab changes without reboot
